        "id": 1006299
      },
      "writtenOn": "2014-01-07T14:24:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In this code block we are about to deliver an ACTION_TIMEZONE_CHANGED broadcast. This is executed in the BroadcastReceiver\u0027s process.\n\nThe problem is that changes to system properties are not instantly visible to all active processes. \n\nInstead of relying on getting the new timezone value from system properties (by calling TimeZone.getDefault() with a null default timezone), we explicitly set it to the value found in extras. The value in extras was added from the value passed in updateTimeZone from the originating process above.\n\nYou are correct that this is a work around for an underlying problem. It could be fixed by:\n* Making changes to system properties synchronized across processes. (Might not even be desirable in all cases)\n* Have the timezone be backed by something other than system properties.\n* Something else...\n\nI made the decision at the time that this change was the best alternative for us.",
      "parentUuid": "4db331fa_172ef4ac",
      "revId": "99991cf808593d94de2c06f46096c0617c96254c",
